        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"no-change-baseline\"><strong>No-Change Baseline</strong></h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">To predict the gene count vectors of perturbed cells, the first method we try is the no-change baseline. For each cell in the perturbed group, this method samples a random cell in the control group and predicts the sample's gene counts. This method makes the assumption that each perturbation will have no effect. This method only uses the validation set, not the training set.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
